\caption{Version 3 Architecture: Analytics-Driven model where facts are computed before reaching the LLM.}
\label{fig:arch_v3}
\end{figure}

Pre-computing statistics reduced LLM reasoning errors, lowered API costs, and accelerated execution. However, the generated text still contained unsupported qualitative commentary (e.g., claiming ``heavy demand from local buyers'').

\subsection{Version 4: Truthfulness Architecture}
Version 4 added a \textbf{Truthfulness Layer} containing post-generation validation. It checked for direct contradictions between the article body and the pre-computed analytics payload. It introduced ``Scope Validation'' to flag articles making geographic assertions outside their assigned target scope. While this successfully caught hallucinations, it lacked granular claim correction, resulting in high rejection rates at the publishing gate.

\subsection{Version 5: Final Architecture (Current)}
The current architecture (Fig.~\ref{fig:arch_v5}) integrates a robust, multi-layered data ingestion system, a pre-computed analytics engine, a grounded LLM prompt module, a claim validation system, and an automated static site publisher.
